oose Queen Mary?\nApplying for a Research Degree\nFunding a PhD\nHow we support you\nGet in touch\nDeadlines\nAssociate Study\nOpen Events\nMasters events\nResearch events\nYour support network\nAccommodation\nFAQs\nQueen Mary University of London\nPostgraduate\nResearch degrees\nSubjects\nResearch degrees in Computer Science\nComputer Science at Queen Mary is part of the wider School of Electronic Engineering and Computer Science. This School has a dynamic community of over 200 PhD students and 80 Post Docs working on cutting-edge research.\nThe research is broadly organised into the following research groups. Please visit the School website for a list of current PhD projects, supervisors and funding opportunities www.eecs.qmul.ac.uk\nAntennas & Electromagnetics\nCentre for Digital Music\nCognitive Science\nCommunication Systems Research\nComputer Vision\nGame AI\nInteractive and Cognitive Environments\nMultimedia & Vision\nNetworks\nOperational Research\nRisk and Information Management\nTheoretical Computer Science\nStaff and students in this School also have the opportunity to work in these three interdisciplinary research centres:\nCentre for Intelligent Sensing\nRobotics - ARQ\nQMEDIA\nHow to Apply\nFull details of how to apply for a PhD in this field can be found here\nCandidates should not apply using the buttons on this page until they have read the application instructions on the School website. It is also strongly advised, although not a formal requirement, to make informal contact with the chosen supervisor before submitting the online application.\nFunding\nhere is a wide range of funding available for PhD study in this field. Individual projects will be advertised on www.findaphd.com and all scholarship opportunities are advertised on our.\nQueen Mary leads an AI + Music (artificial Intelligent and Music) Doctoral Training Programme and more information about this specific funding opportunity can be found here.\nQueen Mary is a new member of the Intelligent Gaming and Gaming Intelligence Doctoral Training Programme and more information about this specific funding opportunity can be found here.\nContact\nMelissa Yeo\nResearch Students Coordinator\nTel: +44 (0)20 7882 5357\nEmail: eecs-phd-enquiries@qmul.ac.uk\nDr Arkaitz Zubaiga\nDirector of Graduate Studies\nEmail: eecs-phd-enquiries@qmul.ac.uk\nApply online\nChoose a degree\nChoose a degree\nMD(Res)\nPhD\nChoose mode of study\nChoose mode of study\nFull-time\nPart-time\nChoose start\nChoose start\nSemester 1 (September start)\nSemester 2 (January start)\nSemester 3 (May start)\nPhD Full-time Interactive and Cognitive Environments - Semester 1 (September Start)PhD Full-time Computer Science - Semester 1 (September Start)PhD Full-time Computer Science - Semester 2 (January Start)PhD Part-time Computer Science - Semester 1 (September Start)PhD Part-time Computer Science - Semester 2 (January Start)\nNo results found.\nFooter navigation\nAccommodation\nAlumni\nSchools and Institutes\nCareers and Employability\nCollaborate with us\nContact\nEvents\nGlobal\nHow to find us\nInternational students\nJobs\nLibrary\nMyQMUL\nNew students\nNews\nOrder a prospectus\nOur brand\nParents\nProfessional services departments\nPublic Engagement\nQMplus\nStaff directory\nStaff intranet\nStrategy 2030\nStudents' Union\nTeachers\nTerm dates\nTrade Union Facility Time\nAccessibility\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy and cookies\nSite map\nModern Slavery Statement\nSupplier fraud alert\nOFS Data\nContact the university\nQueen Mary University of London\nMile End Road\nLondon E1 4NS\n+44 (0) 20 7882 5555\nBack to top\nEdit this page", "links": [["honeypot link", "https://4xvmpmomo3.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/ProdStage"], ["Skip to main content", "https://www.qmul.ac.uk/postgraduate/research/subjects/computer-science.html#main-content"], ["", "https://www.qmul.ac.uk/postgraduate/research/subjects/computer-science.html"], ["Study", "https://www.qmul.ac.uk/postgraduate/research/subjects/computer-s